<div class="import-course-history-guide">
	<div class="ichg-section">
		<p class="ichg-kicker">Workflow A</p>
		<h3 class="ichg-title">New upload</h3>
		<p class="ichg-lead">Use this when you are bringing in legacy course history for the first time, or when you are adding a new import batch.</p>
		<ol class="ichg-steps">
			<li class="ichg-step">
				<div class="ichg-step-body"><strong>Download the template.</strong> On this page, click <strong>Download CSV template</strong> and save the file. You must start from this template (or match its columns exactly) so the import can read your file. Optionally use <strong>Download courses (database)</strong> to export valid <code>course_name</code> values from the system.</div>
			</li>
			<li class="ichg-step">
				<div class="ichg-step-body"><strong>Open the template in a spreadsheet.</strong> Open the file in Excel or another spreadsheet app. You will see <strong>sample rows</strong> that show the correct format: columns, service numbers, course names, and dates. Delete the sample rows once you understand the layout.</div>
			</li>
			<li class="ichg-step">
				<div class="ichg-step-body"><strong>Enter your data.</strong> Replace or add rows with the people and courses to import. <strong>Required:</strong> <code>service_number</code> (or <code>personnel</code>) and <code>course_name</code>. <strong>Optional:</strong> <code>start_date</code>, <code>end_date</code>, <code>grade</code>, <code>personnel_name</code>. Every service number must exist on a <strong>Personnel</strong> record; every course name must match <strong>Course Name</strong> exactly. Save as CSV when finished.</div>
			</li>
			<li class="ichg-step">
				<div class="ichg-step-body"><strong>Upload and submit.</strong> Set <strong>Import batch</strong> to <strong>— New CSV import —</strong>. Click <strong>Upload CSV</strong>, choose your file, and confirm. The table fills with your rows. Rows in <strong>red</strong> already exist in the database (same person and course); fix or remove them. When valid, click <strong>Submit import</strong> to save the batch.</div>
			</li>
		</ol>
	</div>

	<div class="ichg-section">
		<p class="ichg-kicker">Workflow B</p>
		<h3 class="ichg-title">Edit an uploaded batch</h3>
		<p class="ichg-lead">Use this after a batch is saved, when you need to review, correct, or remove records.</p>
		<ol class="ichg-steps">
			<li class="ichg-step">
				<div class="ichg-step-body"><strong>Open the batch.</strong> In <strong>Import batch</strong>, choose <strong>Batch 1</strong>, <strong>Batch 2</strong>, or the batch you need. The table reloads with every row in that import (same columns as after an upload).</div>
			</li>
			<li class="ichg-step">
				<div class="ichg-step-body"><strong>Edit in the system.</strong> Click <strong>Roll over (unlock for editing)</strong>. Then open a row’s <strong>Record</strong> link (or open <strong>Legacy Course Record</strong> from the desk). Change dates, grade, or other allowed fields and save. Repeat for each record you need to fix.</div>
			</li>
			<li class="ichg-step">
				<div class="ichg-step-body"><strong>Delete a single row (while still locked).</strong> If you have <strong>not</strong> rolled over yet, you can click <strong>Remove</strong> on one row to delete only that legacy record. After roll over, use the form or list view to delete if needed.</div>
			</li>
			<li class="ichg-step">
				<div class="ichg-step-body"><strong>Delete the whole batch.</strong> Click <strong>Delete entire batch</strong> to remove every record in that import at once. You will be asked to confirm; this cannot be undone.</div>
			</li>
			<li class="ichg-step">
				<div class="ichg-step-body"><strong>Reset the page.</strong> Click <strong>Clear</strong> to empty the table and reset <strong>Import batch</strong> so you can start a new upload or pick another batch.</div>
			</li>
		</ol>
	</div>
</div>
